Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||08-25-2001||08:26 PM||||Here's a question.  Where can one go, to start looking for a car they used to own ?<P>I'd love to find out what happened to them & possibly contact the new owners.<P>Any ideas ?  Does anyone know to start such a search ?<P>One is a 79 Mercury Capri (Mustang's brother)<P>Thanks for any help<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Capri_e.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-25-2001||09:10 PM||||Boy that would be something. You Know my wife had a liitle mercury capri that was her first car. When she got married her xhusband sold it on her. We have been married for 15 years and she still misses that little car boy would I love to Buy it or one similar to it .But as far as locating the car you would need a vin. # for starters which I dont have.and maybe going to the dmv.Im sure they could track it down but not sure if they would release the info though.Might need a buddy in the police dept. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||08-25-2001||09:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>But as far as locating the car you would need a vin. # for starters ...maybe going to the dmv.Im sure they could track it down but not sure if they would release the info though.Might need a buddy in the police dept. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>10-4 , not a bad idea. Hadn't thought about the DMV.<P>This kind of problem would make a good web site idea to track down things like this.<P>Well, back to the Fiero world.||||reg||6
Z||000003||rockcrawl||08-25-2001||09:38 PM||||A friend of mine just re-purchased the Formula that he bought new in '88. His brother who is a police officer or something tracked it down for him and gave him the name and address of the new owner. He then just went and knocked on the door and said something like, "hey, I remember seeing a Fiero parked here once or twice, I was wondering if you'd like to sell it." Well it worked and he got his old Formula back, although I'm sure what he did was illegal. If you know someone in law enforcement that's willing to break a few rules, it can be done. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||08-25-2001||09:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>A friend of mine just re-purchased the Formula that he bought new in '88.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh wow, that's neat, Bet he's got a big grin/woody over that !<P>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||08-25-2001||11:43 PM||||If you have the vin number, the first thing I'd try is running it through Carfax.<BR>That would at least tell you if it's still on the road and the last city it was registered in. ||||reg||1
